WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:05.580
A bait and switch that was teased in the trailer,&nbsp;
and an altogether different origin from his comic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:10.740
book counterpart. It's time to talk about that&nbsp;
big twist. Major spoilers for "Black Adam" ahead!

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:14.820
Dwayne "The Rock" Johnson has promised a&nbsp;
change of pace for the DC Extended Universe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:19.440
which has so far failed to truly compete&nbsp;
with the Marvel Cinematic Universe. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:23.220
"Black Adam" may not be the success&nbsp;
that Warner Bros. needs it to be. While&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:26.520
the movie debuted to generally&nbsp;
positive responses from fans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:32.520
it has since fallen to a gnarly 42% on Rotten&nbsp;
Tomatoes. Meanwhile, The Verge suggested that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:37.200
the film has an insatiable need to show how cool&nbsp;
murder can be over telling a compelling story.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:41.640
Throughout its two-hour runtime, "Black Adam"&nbsp;
shoves a lot of information at the audience.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:46.920
The movie hits the ground running, opening with&nbsp;
Teth-Adam's supposed origin story, then jumping&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:51.180
ahead to the present day. It's there that we're&nbsp;
introduced to the film's human protagonists,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:56.820
mother and son Adrianna and Amon followed by&nbsp;
supergroup the Justice Society. But the film's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.820 --> 00:01:01.560
most significant plot twist happens during its&nbsp;
numerous flashbacks to the Champion of Kahndaq.

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:05.940
From the beginning, "Black Adam" introduces&nbsp;
audience members to the plotline surrounding the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:12.240
titular anti-hero's origins. The movie opens with&nbsp;
a flashback to 2600 B.C. when the ruthless king&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:17.520
Anh-Kot enslaved the people of Kahndaq, forcing&nbsp;
them to mine the country's natural resource,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:22.740
a powerful substance called Eternium. A young boy&nbsp;
attempts to stage a revolution to free his people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:28.020
from slavery, but Anh-Kot's soldiers capture&nbsp;
the boy and sentence him to death. Before the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:32.580
soldiers can strike the killing blow, the boy&nbsp;
receives the powers of Shazam, becoming the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:37.620
Champion of Kahndaq, which he uses to kill the&nbsp;
king and end his reign, before being entombed.

00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:42.000
The event goes down in Kahndaq's history,&nbsp;
inspiring its citizens as they go through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:46.680
endless phases of occupation by different&nbsp;
forces. It's not until the Justice Society&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:51.360
arrives that we're finally given more details&nbsp;
about the Champion, when Hawkman reveals that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:56.280
Black Adam nearly destroyed Kahndaq, which&nbsp;
resulted in his imprisonment, not entombment.

00:01:56.280 --> 00:02:00.480
Later in the film, Black Adam reveals that&nbsp;
he's not the legendary Champion of Kahndaq.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:05.340
The young boy that fueled the nation's revolution&nbsp;
and received the powers of Shazam was, in fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:10.860
Adam's son, Hurut. As the Champion, Hurut was&nbsp;
invincible, so the king's men attacked his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:15.540
family instead. To save his father from certain&nbsp;
death, Hurut transferred his powers to Adam.

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:18.540
"My son sacrificed his life to save me."

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:24.180
Unfortunately, this gave the assassins the&nbsp;
opportunity they needed to kill Hurut. A&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:27.720
rage-filled Adam uses his new powers&nbsp;
to get revenge for his son's death,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:31.980
destroying most of Kahndaq before being&nbsp;
brought in front of the wizards of Shazam.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:35.880
The wizards deem him unworthy to hold&nbsp;
the powers and imprison him for eternity.

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:41.040
"Black Adam" takes much of its inspiration&nbsp;
from DC Comics' New 52 run of the character,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:44.400
though the comic book origin is a&nbsp;
bit darker than Dwayne Johnson's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:47.760
portrayal. While Johnson's comic&nbsp;
book counterpart doesn't have a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:51.900
son named Hurut, his nephew Aman played&nbsp;
a significant role in his origin story.

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:56.880
In the newly reset DC Universe, Black Adam&nbsp;
was given a new spin on his origin story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.880 --> 00:03:02.160
in "Justice League Volume 2". This version of&nbsp;
Teth-Adam was also enslaved in ancient Kahndaq,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:07.200
where the nation's dictator murdered his&nbsp;
entire family, leaving only his nephew,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:11.580
Aman. During their escape, Adam receives a&nbsp;
life-threatening injury before the Wizard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:16.080
Shazam transports the two to the Rock of&nbsp;
Eternity. There, the wizard deems Aman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:21.540
worthy of the powers of Shazam, tasking him with&nbsp;
freeing Kahndaq. Aman agrees, but only if the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:25.980
wizard heals Adam. Aman receives the powers,&nbsp;
and the wizard heals and strengthens Adam.

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:27.660
"I kneel before no-one."

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:31.920
Adam and Aman travel back to Kahndaq&nbsp;
but disagree about how to use their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:36.060
newly acquired powers. While Adam wants&nbsp;
to exact revenge by killing the dictator,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.600 --> 00:03:40.320
Aman seeks a more peaceful solution.&nbsp;
Fearing that Aman's plan won't work,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:45.120
Adam kills his nephew and steals his powers,&nbsp;
claiming he did it for the greater good.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:50.040
He becomes the Mighty Adam and goes down in&nbsp;
history as the champion that freed Kahndaq.

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:54.720
Similar to "Black Adam," the comics say that&nbsp;
the Champion disappeared. However, Adam turned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:59.280
against the Council of Eternity that gave him&nbsp;
his powers and killed them. The Wizard Shazam,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:04.200
the only surviving member, manages to imprison&nbsp;
him, subsequently dubbing him Black Adam.

